Subject: [PATCH 042/148] feat(registry): publish gauntlet-tdd 0.1.0 (gcp-dnxq)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Second half of the two-commit publish sequence. validate_registry.py does not
trust the hash in the file: it recomputes it from `git ls-tree` over the pack
subtree at the named commit and fails when it cannot ("a hash that cannot be
computed is an error, never a pass"). So the subtree has to exist in history
before it can be pinned, which is why this is a separate commit and why
`commit` names c84a27b — the commit that INTRODUCED the pack — rather than
this one.

The entry was produced by `make registry-publish PACK=gauntlet-tdd
PACK_PATH=gauntlet-tdd VERSION=0.1.0 REGISTRY_COMMIT=c84a27b...`, but only
the gauntlet-tdd block is kept. `gc pack release stamp` also rewrote all
fifteen pre-existing [[pack]] entries to add `tier = "community"` and
`publisher = "Unknown publisher"`; that churn is unrelated to this bead, no
existing entry carries those keys, and validate_registry.py does not require
them, so registry.toml was restored and the new entry appended by hand. The
diff is additive: 13 insertions, 0 deletions.

Validation:
- `python3 validate_registry.py registry.toml` -> `registry.toml: ok`
- `python3 validate_registry.py --require-git` (the CI form, which is what
  actually recomputes the subtree hash) -> `registry.toml: ok`
- tests/test_validate_registry.py + test_registry_release.py +
  test_pack_release_compat.py -> 36 passed
---
 registry.toml | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/registry.toml b/registry.toml
index 3c9c59e4..381c1d5c 100644
--- a/registry.toml
+++ b/registry.toml
@@ -368,3 +368,15 @@ schema = 1
     commit = "510a4e22a34d325063fe24f77038c004221b7e7e"
     hash = "sha256:e4d85af1e0e202e30785ac33ac12c83f26dba1cc61de22573d3ac5f8ea9e80de"
     description = "First release under the new name; the pack was renamed from contributing. Carries everything since contributing 0.2.1: the mol-contributing-* formula set, renamed lifecycle skills with an orchestrated umbrella, default-branch resolution from the local ref, and bead commands routed through gc. Imports must switch from //contributing to //contributing-to-gascity."
+[[pack]]
+  name = "gauntlet-tdd"
+  description = "The gauntlet RED-to-GREEN contract loop as a pack: scaffold a .bats contract from a bead's acceptance criteria, prove it red with gauntlet lint, route implementation to the rig's implementer, prove it green with a bead-scoped run (mol-tdd-red-green)."
+  source = "https://github.com/gastownhall/gascity-packs/tree/main/gauntlet-tdd"
+  source_kind = "git"
+
+  [[pack.release]]
+    version = "0.1.0"
+    ref = "main"
+    commit = "c84a27ba9bc290f67cbf24ba86e663e7268d6798"
+    hash = "sha256:3e93803831adc79d19da3d9bb06e9bc23518d1013ab1432da81a4d18b40de7ff"
+    description = "Initial gauntlet-tdd release: the RED-to-GREEN contract loop as one formula (mol-tdd-red-green) plus a wrapper command, pinned to the bats lane with gauntlet lint as the red gate."
